            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "If I recall correctly, the only animation enabled in MiniMax *is* from 'mini.indentscope'. And yes, it [can be disabled](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/3923662bf3d6ca49a9503f8d7196ea0450983e6a/doc/mini-indentscope.txt#L128).\r\n\r\nIn particular, here is one way to do it:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nlater(function()\r\n  require('mini.indentscope').setup({\r\n    draw = {\r\n      animation = function() return 0 end,\r\n    },\r\n  })\r\nend)\r\n```\r\n\r\nA more explicit approach can also be like this:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nlater(function()\r\n  local indentscope = require('mini.indentscope')\r\n  indentscope.setup({\r\n    draw = {\r\n      animation = indentscope.gen_animation.none(),\r\n    },\r\n  })\r\nend)\r\n```",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">If I recall correctly, the only animation enabled in MiniMax <em>is</em> from 'mini.indentscope'. And yes, it <a href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/3923662bf3d6ca49a9503f8d7196ea0450983e6a/doc/mini-indentscope.txt#L128\">can be disabled</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">In particular, here is one way to do it:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"later(function()\n  require('mini.indentscope').setup({\n    draw = {\n      animation = function() return 0 end,\n    },\n  })\nend)\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-c1\">later</span>(<span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>()\n  <span class=\"pl-c1\">require</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>mini.indentscope<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>).<span class=\"pl-c1\">setup</span>({\n    <span class=\"pl-smi\">draw</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> {\n      <span class=\"pl-en\">animation</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>() <span class=\"pl-k\">return</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">0</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>,\n    },\n  })\n<span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>)</pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">A more explicit approach can also be like this:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"later(function()\n  local indentscope = require('mini.indentscope')\n  indentscope.setup({\n    draw = {\n      animation = indentscope.gen_animation.none(),\n    },\n  })\nend)\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-c1\">later</span>(<span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>()\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">indentscope</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">require</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>mini.indentscope<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>)\n  <span class=\"pl-smi\">indentscope</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">setup</span>({\n    <span class=\"pl-smi\">draw</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> {\n      <span class=\"pl-smi\">animation</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">indentscope</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">gen_animation</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">none</span>(),\n    },\n  })\n<span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>)</pre></div>",
            "bodyText": "If I recall correctly, the only animation enabled in MiniMax is from 'mini.indentscope'. And yes, it can be disabled.\nIn particular, here is one way to do it:\nlater(function()\n  require('mini.indentscope').setup({\n    draw = {\n      animation = function() return 0 end,\n    },\n  })\nend)\nA more explicit approach can also be like this:\nlater(function()\n  local indentscope = require('mini.indentscope')\n  indentscope.setup({\n    draw = {\n      animation = indentscope.gen_animation.none(),\n    },\n  })\nend)",
